# Normalize line endings on checkout to avoid Windows CRLF drift
# showing every file as "modified" in `git status`.
#
# * text=auto: git detects text files and normalizes them to LF in the
#   repo. On Windows checkouts they get CRLF; on macOS/Linux they get
#   LF. Either way the working tree matches what the platform expects
#   and git status stays clean.
* text=auto

# Lua and TOC source: force LF everywhere. WoW loads either fine, but
# LF-only avoids any diff churn if the file gets edited on Windows
# with an editor that respects .gitattributes (VS Code, Sublime, etc.).
*.lua   text eol=lf
*.toc   text eol=lf
*.xml   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf

# Windows-native files: force CRLF so a Unix checkout doesn't strip
# them (cmd.exe requires CRLF in .bat files).
*.bat   text eol=crlf

# Binary formats: never touch.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.tga   binary
*.blp   binary
*.ogg   binary
*.mp3   binary
*.zip   binary
